// The boundary between the scrim control plane (Go) and data plane (Rust),
// design D12.
//
// Transport: gRPC over one end of a socketpair the control plane creates and
// the data plane inherits (D11). The data plane is the gRPC server; the
// control plane is the only client. Nothing else can reach the socket.
//
// Off the hot path: the control plane pushes versioned snapshots and the data
// plane decides allow and deny locally. Only Asks waits on the control plane,
// and only for requests a rule sends to a human.
//
// Versioning: every top-level message carries `protocol` as field 1. Each side
// refuses a message whose protocol differs from its own PROTOCOL_VERSION
// (status FAILED_PRECONDITION), and the control plane refuses to start a data
// plane whose Hello reports a different one. A change that an older peer
// would misread bumps PROTOCOL_VERSION; both sides and their tests change in
// the same commit.
//
// Secrets: ValueEntry.value, PlaceholderKey.key, CaptureRequest.value,
// CaCertificate.key_pem and UpstreamProxy.password are the only fields that
// hold secret material (with AskCaller.kubernetes_token and
// RedactRequest.text, see AGENTS.md).
// Generated debug printers for those messages are replaced by redacting ones
// on both sides; neither may be logged, echoed in an error or copied into an
// event.

